<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <Description>The application layer of a .NET service over MediatR: commands, queries and their handlers, the pipeline around them (tracing, logging, metrics, authorization, validation, idempotency, transactions, auditing) in one fixed order, and the bridge that turns a domain event into a MediatR notification.

One call registers it: services.AddSharedKernelApplication(typeof(Program).Assembly, app => app.WithAuthorization().WithTransactions()) scans the assembly for handlers and FluentValidation validators, turns on tracing, logging, metrics and validation, and adds the behaviors you opt into. A service a behavior needs is checked when the host starts, so registration order does not matter.

Every handler returns Result or Result&lt;T&gt;, so an expected failure is a value the caller must handle rather than an exception thrown past it. Authorization is declared once, on the use case, with [RequirePermission]. Only a successful outcome persists anything: a failed Result commits nothing and releases its idempotency key. Depends on SharedKernel.Application.Abstractions, SharedKernel.Primitives, SharedKernel.Domain, MediatR 12.4.1 (the last MIT-licensed release, pinned deliberately), FluentValidation and first-party Microsoft.Extensions packages.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>First release as one package: the former SharedKernel.Application.Behaviors was merged into it (P-563).

WHAT IS IN IT
- Commands and queries: ICommand, ICommand&lt;T&gt;, IQuery&lt;T&gt;, ICommandBase, IQueryBase, the handler aliases, IStreamQuery&lt;T&gt; and IStreamQueryHandler&lt;,&gt;.
- Registration: AddSharedKernelApplication(assemblies, app => …) with WithAuthorization(), WithIdempotency(), WithTransactions(), WithAuditing() and WithBehavior(type, PipelineStage).
- Request declarations: [RequirePermission], IIdempotentRequest, IAuditableRequest&lt;TResponse&gt;, ILoggableRequest&lt;TResponse&gt;, and ICommandScope for work after the commit.
- Domain events: IDomainEventHandler&lt;T&gt;, DomainEventNotification&lt;T&gt;, AddDomainEventHandler&lt;,&gt;().
- For idempotency stores (SharedKernel.Application.Idempotency): IRequestIdempotencyStore, IdempotencyBeginResult, IdempotencyBeginStatus.

See the package README for the pipeline, the failure matrix and the full reference.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>cqrs;mediatr;application;command;query;pipeline-behavior;validation;authorization;idempotency;transaction;auditing;domain-events;shared-kernel</PackageTags>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);nullable;CS1591;RS0016;RS0017;RS0022;RS0024;RS0025;RS0036;RS0037</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Layering ceiling for SharedKernel.Application is 01.Core, 03.Domain, 04.Contracts and
      SharedKernel.Application.Abstractions. It never references 06.Persistence, 07.Messaging,
      12.Security, or SharedKernel.Caching.Abstractions (that reference belongs to
      SharedKernel.Application.Caching only).
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\01.Core\SharedKernel.Primitives\SharedKernel.Primitives.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\03.Domain\SharedKernel.Domain\SharedKernel.Domain.csproj" />
    <!-- IRequestContext, IUnitOfWork and IAuditTrailWriter: the contracts 06.Persistence implements
         directly, so no composition-root adapter is needed. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SharedKernel.Application.Abstractions\SharedKernel.Application.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      MediatR pinned to 12.4.x — the last MIT-licensed major (v13 introduced a commercial
      license). This is a deliberate platform ceiling; see CLAUDE.md version-pin callout.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <!-- Concrete AddLogging(): the registration call makes ILogger<T> resolvable even against a bare
         ServiceCollection. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <!-- ValidateDataAnnotations()/ValidateOnStart() for ApplicationLoggingOptions and the start-time
         seam check. A plain Microsoft.Extensions.* package, never a SharedKernel.Configuration reference. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.DataAnnotations" />
    <!-- IMeterFactory / services.AddMetrics() for the metrics behavior. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The behaviors are internal; the test project constructs them directly. -->
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
      <_Parameter1>SharedKernel.Application.Tests</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" PrivateAssets="all" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Shipped.txt" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
